ncrewed hull, who never fell through anything. The screen would state a cause that did not happen.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"corrected\": {\n        \"cause\": \"The astronaut touched terrain while not aboard the ship. How you got there does not change it — a slow fall that never got hot, or a step away from a hull parked on the ground. Landed needs the pilot aboard.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"stranded_d\",\n      \"verdict\": \"revise\",\n      \"issues\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"contradicts_gdd\",\n          \"quote\": \"STRANDED\",\n          \"evidence\": \"[2.7b] \\\"(d) ship staged, chute shredded, on a descent whose minimum achievable touchdown speed exceeds the destruction cap — a conservative closed-form check, like the lamps — resolved immediately as 0 HP rather than flown out in real time.\\\"\",\n          \"cites\": [\"2.7b\", \"2.7a\"],\n          \"why\": \"Clause (d) is a branch of the unwinnability check, but the document says it resolves as 0 HP, not as stranded. Since every reachable end state resolves to exactly one outcome (§2.7), a screen headed STRANDED names the wrong one — and the item's own rule_broken already says the check resolves it as 0 HP, so the screen contradicts itself as well as the passage.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"corrected\": {\n        \"title\": \"SHIP DESTROYED\",\n        \"cause\": \"Staged, chute shredded, and the lowest touchdown speed still reachable was past the destruction cap. The check called it there rather than making you fly the fall out.\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}","ttft_ms":59923,"ttft_stream_ms":1305,"time_to_request_ms":339,"type":"result","duration_ms":73878,"uuid":"b7bf7ec5-bc2a-4dca-b934-2f6e04f3c7db"}
